course: dictionary
lesson: 2685
title: The dictionary: your word helper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary is a book or website that lists words in alphabetical order, so you can find a word quickly. Each entry tells you what the word means, how to spell it and how to say it. When you are not sure of a word, your teacher will say, «look it up in the dictionary».
explain: Some dictionaries help with two languages. A bilingual dictionary, such as an English–French one, gives a word in one language and its meaning in the other. A picture dictionary uses pictures to show what a word means, which helps when you are learning to read.
explain: Dictionaries also record how people write. «American spelling dropped the u from words like "color" and "favorite"», helped by Noah Webster's dictionary of 1828, while Britain kept «colour» and «favourite». Both spellings are correct in their own country.
fact: A dictionary lists words in alphabetical order.
fact: Each dictionary entry can tell you a word's meaning, spelling and pronunciation.
fact: A bilingual dictionary, such as an English–French one, gives meanings in two languages.
fact: In computing, a dictionary is a list of names paired with values in a computer program.
fact: «Rizz» means charm; it is slang that has settled down enough to be listed in some dictionaries.
exercise: What order does a dictionary list its words in? | Random order | Order of colour | *Alphabetical order | Order of length
exercise: «Maya used a bilingual dictionary to read the French menu.» What kind of dictionary did Maya use? | A dictionary of rhymes | *A dictionary that gives meanings in two languages | A picture dictionary | A dictionary of numbers only
exercise: «American spelling dropped the u from "color", but Britain kept "colour".» Why are both spellings correct? | *Each is correct in its own country | Only one spelling is ever right | Dictionaries cannot record spelling | The u is always silent
test: What does a dictionary entry tell you about a word? | Who wrote the book | The price of the book | The number of pages it has | *Its meaning, spelling and pronunciation
test: In computing, what is a dictionary? | A cooking recipe | A type of computer keyboard | *A list of names paired with values in a computer program | A map of the internet
exam: «Slang moves fast, but some of it ends up in dictionaries, like "rizz".» Why would slang like «rizz» appear in a dictionary? | Because teachers wrote it on the board | Because it is spelled with a z | *Because it became common and settled down, so people kept using it | Dictionaries only list old words
